From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:13:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: meson-gx: add amlogic,tx-phase property

The TX clock phase is hardcoded to 0 degrees with the core phase at 180.
On Amlogic S7 this is exactly the only failing combination for the eMMC
at 52 MHz: the first CMD6 sent at 50 MHz gets a response CRC error and
the card does not initialise. A scan of the core and TX phases shows that
only the TX phase 180 degrees away from the core phase fails. The SD
controller of the same SoC on the other hand needs the default phase,
with TX at 180 degrees writes to the SD card fail.

Add an optional amlogic,tx-phase property (degrees) to set the TX phase
per controller, the default stays 0. With 180 degrees on the S7 eMMC
reads of 6 GiB at 52 MHz give identical checksums and no CRC errors.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c
index d2b9b5d..451679a 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c
@@ -438,16 +438,25 @@ static int meson_mmc_clk_init(struct meson_host *host)
 	struct clk_mux *mux;
 	struct clk_divider *div;
 	char clk_name[32];
+	u32 tx_phase = 0;
 	int i, ret = 0;
 	const char *mux_parent_names[MUX_CLK_NUM_PARENTS];
 	const char *clk_parent[1];
 	u32 clk_reg;
 
+	/* Optional TX clock phase in degrees, 0 by default */
+	device_property_read_u32(host->dev, "amlogic,tx-phase", &tx_phase);
+	if (tx_phase % 90 || tx_phase > 270) {
+		dev_warn(host->dev, "invalid amlogic,tx-phase %u, using 0\n",
+			 tx_phase);
+		tx_phase = 0;
+	}
+
 	/* init SD_EMMC_CLOCK to sane defaults w/min clock rate */
 	clk_reg = CLK_ALWAYS_ON(host);
 	clk_reg |= CLK_DIV_MASK;
 	clk_reg |= FIELD_PREP(CLK_CORE_PHASE_MASK, CLK_PHASE_180);
-	clk_reg |= FIELD_PREP(CLK_TX_PHASE_MASK, CLK_PHASE_0);
+	clk_reg |= FIELD_PREP(CLK_TX_PHASE_MASK, tx_phase / 90);
 	clk_reg |= FIELD_PREP(CLK_RX_PHASE_MASK, CLK_PHASE_0);
 	if (host->mmc->caps & MMC_CAP_SDIO_IRQ)
 		clk_reg |= CLK_IRQ_SDIO_SLEEP(host);
-- 
